---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About Us"
  description="Who makes Study Timer Online, why it exists, what the tools do, and how we decide what to build next."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <section class="page-band" style="padding-block: 3rem 6rem;">
    <div class="container-page" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <article class="card legal-copy" style="padding: clamp(28px, 6vw, 56px); border-radius: 28px; line-height: 1.8;">
        <header style="margin-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--brand-a15); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; color: var(--content-heading); margin: 0; line-height: 1.2;">About Study Timer Online</h1>
        </header>

        <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
        <p>Study Timer Online started from a simple frustration. Most online timers were either bare countdowns with nothing to help you use them well, or productivity apps that wanted an account before you could start a 25-minute session. We wanted something you could open, set and start in a few seconds, that remembered your progress without asking who you are.</p>

        <h2>What you can do here</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/timer">Study timer</a>: a countdown with preset and custom lengths, full-screen mode and optional voice cues. Good for focus blocks and timed practice papers.</li>
          <li><a href="/pomodoro">Pomodoro timer</a>: alternating focus and break periods, with a longer break after four rounds. All lengths are adjustable.</li>
          <li><a href="/study-planner">Planner</a>: a short queue of today's tasks so you always know what's next.</li>
          <li><a href="/study-stats">Stats</a>: your daily study minutes, a 21-day heatmap, time per subject and your current streak.</li>
          <li><a href="/guides">Study guides</a>: practical articles on session length, the Pomodoro Technique, mock exams, active recall and daily planning.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we build it</h2>
        <p>We keep the tools small and quick. Everything you create (settings, tasks, sessions) is saved in your own browser, so there's nothing to sign up for and nothing for us to lose. The guides are written for students who want to study better, not just longer. Wherever we mention research, we name the study so you can look it up yourself.</p>
        <p>The site is free. We use analytics to see which pages are useful, and ads may appear to cover running costs. Details are in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>Study Timer Online is an independent project from Mindset Clarity, the same small team that makes <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.daystair.app" rel="noopener">Daystair</a>, a goal-based study planner for Android. We use these tools for our own study and work, which is how most of the features came about.</p>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>Feature ideas, bug reports and corrections to the guides are always welcome. Send them through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
